<title>FRANCE: Bouygues breaks even in property arm.</title>
<headline>Bouygues breaks even in property arm.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>French construction company Bouygues said on Tuesday its property division broke even in 1996 with an estimated 15 million franc profit, after a loss of 845 million in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;Thanks to favourable government measures, house sales showed a strong rise in 1996 compared to 1995, up 20 percent in volume and 26 percent in turnover,&quot; the company said in a statement with 1996 results.</p>
</text>
